A||||7||Phil||Auto shift knob||||1||
Z||000000||Phil||02-04-2000||10:18 AM||||My son has expressed a desire to change out the shift knob on his 88GT automatic. A quick check shows the selection to be quite limited. Anybody with some suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||02-04-2000||12:59 PM||||Check out the shifter knobs on other GM cars. GM is too cheap to reinvent the shifter knob so most if not all of them will fit a Fiero. I was looking for a new knob for my manual but all the aftermarket stuff looks so stupid. But I saw a Camaro shifter knob and got one from the dealer. $50 later I have a knob that is different from everybody elses and looks completely stock! Just a suggestion.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-04-2000||04:15 PM||||Funny a Camaro was mentioned.  I bought a leather auto shift knob at my local boneyard out of a late model Camaro for $10.  Perfect condition.  They sell brand new at the dealer for $48 and change.  Your boneyard can be your friend.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||02-04-2000||04:55 PM||||Its been a long while since Ive been to the local boneyard. Its my day off I think I have somewhere to go now!||||reg||14
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||02-05-2000||04:20 AM||||Paid off to go to the boneyard! I have been looking to get some front wheel wells that won't cost much and I found a Fiero in the yard with them intact! When I changed the GT nose to a Formula I didn't have the correct wheel wells and the GT wells were pretty beat up to begin with. I got both sides for $13.83!!!!<P>You Da Man Monkeyman!||||reg||6
Z||000005||Oreif||02-05-2000||01:46 PM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/psside.jpg">   <BR>Here's a picture of mine. I ordered it from Pontiac. It is a 1996 Bonneville SSEi shifter handle (not the leather one)It was $8.00. The leather one was $48!<P>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-05-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||02-06-2000||06:45 PM||||WKDFIRO--I occasionally have a good idea or two.<BR>Oreif--Looks good although I prefer leather and something a little smaller.  Yours seems to have the correct angle when it's in park.  Was that intentional or an accident?  What's the part # in case anyone else is interested?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||02-07-2000||12:07 AM||||The angle of the shifter is how it is naturally. The clip that holds it on only goes on one way. That is why I picked the Bonneville one, the Sunfire one was straight. This is due to the angle of the shifter in relation to the drivers seat in the vehicles. As for part number I don't know what it is I just went to the parts counter and asked for the handle. I know the top looks big but it actually is just right for me. I tend to hold it like a joystick  with  a finger on the button rather than on top. It's more comfortable this way since the center console is high.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-07-2000).]||||reg||1
